BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250528
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250529
DTSTAMP:20261005T191706Z
UID:04srmop3gat2all2pagb34794o@google.com
CREATED:20250507T150324Z
DESCRIPTION:<p dir="ltr">We will be doing our Valleyfair performance on Wed
 nesday\, May 28th. We have chosen to attend the same day as the 8th-grade f
 ield trip! 8th graders in music ensembles will ride the music buses\, but w
 ill be able to meet up with the rest of the 8th-grade students once we arri
 ve. We do this because the ticket is less expensive for a performer.</p><br
 ><p dir="ltr"><u>A permission slip is required to attend. Please </u>sign<u
 > and return the form NO LATER than </u><b><u>May 19th</u></b> Link to perm
 ission slip: <a href="https://forms.gle/qPdFHBiXQANz4Y5f6" target="_blank">
 https://forms.gle/<wbr />qPdFHBiXQANz4Y5f6</a></p><p>Seniors are invited to
  attend and perform with the ensembles. They still need a permission slip\,
  so please fill out a form for senior students so that we know how many stu
 dents we have.</p><br><p dir="ltr"><i>Seniors can drive themselves as they 
 will have graduated\, but still need a permission slip and transportation f
 orm. All other students need to ride the bus.</i></p><br><p dir="ltr">There
  will be two options for bus departure times. Students must take the bus th
 at they sign up for on the permission slip. No changes are allowed.</p><p d
 ir="ltr">First bus will leave Valleyfair at 1:45 to return to Hill-Murray a
 t about 2:40</p><p dir="ltr">The other buses will leave Valleyfair at 5:30 
 to return to Hill-Murray at about 6:30 (depending on traffic)</p><br><p dir
 ="ltr">Tickets are $28 for performers and will be applied to your TADS (tui
 tion) account - this is the cost for the ticket <u>only</u> and does not in
 clude food/beverage/other purchases. Valleyfair is cashless\, so students w
 ill need to bring an electronic way to pay for food.  If they want souvenir
 s\, carnival games\, and/or the arcade\, they are all extra money. Lunch is
  on your own and at your leisure (but staying with your student group\, of 
 course).  The water park is closed.  Two buses and trailers will stay for i
 nstruments only. You will only have access directly before or after your pe
 rformance. </p><br><p dir="ltr">Wear appropriate shorts/pants (must fit HM 
 guidelines) with black HM polos. Students are welcome to bring their polo a
 nd put it on over their top when we get instruments from the bus before the
  performance\, then leave it on the bus when we put instruments back. If th
 ey wish\, they may wear their polos all day.</p><br><p dir="ltr">Itinerary<
 /p><p dir="ltr">8:10am - load buses/trailers</p><p dir="ltr">8:30am - Depar
 t </p><p dir="ltr">9:30am - Arrival/Park Opens</p><p dir="ltr">We will show
  students where to meet up before the performance when we arrive.</p><br><p
  dir="ltr"><u>Performance Line-Up-</u></p><p dir="ltr">11:35 Choirs</p><p d
 ir="ltr">12:00 Bands</p><p dir="ltr">12:25 Orchestra</p><br><p dir="ltr">De
 pending on which bus students ride home\, there will be specific informatio
 n about when and where to meet before heading to the bus. We will communica
 te this to students when we arrive.</p><br><p dir="ltr">Bus 1 departs Valle
 yfair at 1:45 to return to Hill-Murray at about 2:40</p><p dir="ltr">Buses 
 2 and 3 will leave Valleyfair at 5:30 to return to Hill-Murray at about 6:3
 0</p><br><p dir="ltr">Students: You are representing Hill-Murray School at 
 all times.  You are expected to follow all school rules and codes of conduc
 t when you are “on the road” at performance sites.  We want to be invited b
 ack! </p><br><p dir="ltr"><u>You must stay with your chosen student group o
 f 3 - 4 students at all times</u>. Please plan your group wisely. If you do
  not like big coasters\, you should probably not join a group of people who
  like big coasters unless you are content waiting for them.  Stay with your
  music family and do not leave anyone alone\, ever.  We always watch out fo
 r and take care of our HM family!  Be kind and polite. No group member exch
 anges\, returns\, swaps\, or refunds - stay with your group. </p><br><p dir
 ="ltr">Helpful tips:</p><ol><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Wear sunscreen </p><
 /li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Wear clothes that have a zipper pocket </p><
 /li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Keep your money and phone in the zipper pock
 et (and remember to zip it)</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Wear comfort
 able shoes that tie or velcro</p></li><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Most rides
  do not allow unsecured items.  Avoid bringing a purse or handbag. </p></li
 ><li dir="ltr"><p dir="ltr">Do not leave your bag\, instrument\, or case un
 attended in the park at any time. This will prevent theft and prevent the p
 ark’s security team from needing to come and take your item for security re
 asons. </p></li></ol><br><p dir="ltr">Helpful numbers: </p><p dir="ltr">Get
  all the phone numbers of the people in your group</p><p dir="ltr">Get your
  teacher’s number as well. </p><br><p dir="ltr">Notes from Valleyfair:</p><
 p dir="ltr">For your safety\, all guests must proceed through metal detecti
 on and security checks prior to entering the park. If you exit\, you must b
 e rescreened.</p><p dir="ltr">Sorry\, NO OUTSIDE FOOD OR BEVERAGE (with the
  exception of water) is allowed inside Valleyfair. </p><p dir="ltr">Guests 
 may leave the park and re-enter by getting their hand stamped at the re-adm
 ission turnstile before exiting and presenting their ticket stub at the tim
 e of re-entry into the park.</p><p dir="ltr">Extra spending money will be n
 eeded for food\, merchandise and games. RipCord and Dinosaurs Alive! are no
 t included in park admission and require separate fees.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250513T154338Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Valleyfair 
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
